@startuml seq_s2_grant_permission
title Sequence — Granting a permission to a role

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam actorBorderColor #808080
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #808080
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam databaseBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceReferenceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #808080
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam TitleFontSize 13
skinparam TitleFontColor #333333
autonumber

actor "Administrator" as Admin
participant "Angular SPA" as SPA
participant "RoleController" as RC
participant "RoleService" as RS
participant "UserService" as US
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
actor "Holder of the role" as U

Admin -> SPA : tick a permission on a role
SPA -> RC : PUT /api/roles/{id}/permissions
RC -> RS : updatePermissions(roleId, codes)
note right of RC
  @PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('MANAGE_ROLES')")
  The check names the permission, never the role.
end note

RS -> DB : replace the role_permissions rows
DB --> RS : ok
RS -> US : bump tokenVersion of every holder
US -> DB : UPDATE users SET token_version = token_version + 1
DB --> US : ok
RS --> RC : updated role
RC --> SPA : 200
SPA --> Admin : new matrix displayed

== next request from a holder of the role ==

U -> SPA : open a screen
SPA -> RC : any authenticated call
RC --> SPA : 401 Unauthorized
SPA --> U : sign in again, new rights applied

note over RS, DB
  The policy is a table. Granting a right changes data,
  never code, and takes effect without redeployment.
end note

@enduml
